# k.http.HttpClient on the server against the fake API of fakes.toml
# (docs/design/32-http-client.md): responses whatever their status, the
# four HttpError cases, typed statuses, and what reaches the third party.

### fetchJson decodes a 2xx JSON body, with @JsonKey
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Describe
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/forecast", "timeoutMs": 5000}
>>> 200
json {"value": "forecast 21.5 C"}

### a 5xx is .status with the third party's body
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Describe
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/down", "timeoutMs": 5000}
>>> 200
json {"value": "status 503 Service Unavailable"}

### a 4xx is .status too
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Describe
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/missing", "timeoutMs": 5000}
>>> 200
json {"value": "status 404 no such place"}

### a body that isn't JSON is .decoding
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Describe
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/not-json", "timeoutMs": 5000}
>>> 200
json {"value": "decoding"}

### JSON of the wrong shape is .decoding
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Describe
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/wrong-shape", "timeoutMs": 5000}
>>> 200
json {"value": "decoding"}

### a slow answer is .timeout
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Describe
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/slow", "timeoutMs": 200}
>>> 200
json {"value": "timeout"}

### send returns a non-2xx response as a response, with a named status
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Raw
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/down"}
>>> 200
json {"value": "503 success=false named=true Service Unavailable"}

### a code without a name is .other
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Raw
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/teapot"}
>>> 200
json {"value": "418 success=false named=false short and stout"}

### an unmatched path is the fake's 404
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Raw
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{"path": "/v1/nothing"}
>>> 200
json {"value": "404 success=false named=false no fake route"}

### a refused connection is .offline
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Unreachable
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": "offline"}

### the method, query, headers, bearer token and form body reach the API
POST /httpc.upstream.UpstreamProtocol/Create
content-type: application/json
connect-protocol-version: 1

{}
>>> 200
json {"value": "t_1 POST /v1/things?expand=all auth=Bearer sk_test_123 key=thing-1 type=application/x-www-form-urlencoded body=name=K%20Mug&quantity=2"}
